---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Adrian Lee | Community Ecosystem Strategist, Certified AI Governance Professional. 17+ years of experience leading global communities, developer ecosystems, and operations at OKX, Binance, Google, Wargaming, and IAHGames."
>

  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="page-header__eyebrow">
          <div class="section-label"><span class="label">About</span></div>
        </div>
        <h1 class="page-header__title">
          The person behind<br>
          <em>the playbook.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="page-header__desc">
          Community strategist, platform safety practitioner, and AI governance professional. 
          I have spent over 17 years inside global digital platforms and gaming ecosystems, 
          learning why communities hold together and why they break.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- BIO SECTION -->
    <section class="bio section" aria-labelledby="bio-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="bio__grid">

          <div class="bio__photo-col">
            <div class="bio__photo-wrap">
              <img
                src="/images/adrian-lee.jpg"
                alt="Adrian Lee"
                width="440"
                height="560"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="bio__social">
              <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/adrianlee" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="about-linkedin">
                LinkedIn ↗
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bio__text-col">
            <h2 id="bio-heading">Background</h2>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>
                I did not start as a conventional community manager. I started by troubleshooting 
                why online spaces repeatedly fall apart when they grow.
              </p>
              <p>
                My early work in gaming operations at <strong>IAHGames</strong> showed me that 
                communities do not simply organize themselves into healthy spaces. They need clear 
                operating rules: practical rituals, aligned incentives, realistic moderation, 
                and rapid feedback loops. Without these, platforms suffer toxicity, rapid user turnover, 
                and loss of trust. With them, users stick around and take ownership of the space.
              </p>
              <p>
                I brought those lessons to larger and more volatile platforms: developer ecosystem programs across 13 countries at <strong>Google</strong>, live gaming communities at <strong>Wargaming</strong>, and global crypto exchange ecosystems at <strong>Binance</strong> and <strong>OKX</strong>, 
                where operational mistakes carry direct financial consequences.
              </p>
              <p>
                Along the way, I saw a familiar issue repeating in generative AI: teams deploying autonomous 
                agents were making the exact mistakes social networks made a decade ago. Governance was treated 
                as an afterthought. Escalations were unmanaged. When edge cases hit, the operational 
                team was caught unprepared.
              </p>
              <p>
                That insight led me directly into AI governance. Managing community platforms and governing 
                AI systems solve the exact same core challenge: how to build human and automated systems 
                that remain reliable under heavy, unpredictable use.
              </p>
              <p>
                Today, I advise organizations on community architecture, platform trust and safety, 
                and practical AI governance. I completed the <strong>Certified AI Governance Professional (AIGP)</strong> programme through SMU Academy (jointly certified with the AI Verify Foundation and endorsed by IMDA), focusing on actionable operational systems over abstract corporate theory.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- VALUES -->
    <section class="values section--sm" aria-labelledby="values-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Operating principles</span></div>
        <h2 id="values-heading">Principles that guide the work</h2>

        <div class="values__grid">
          <div class="value__card card">
            <div class="value__number">01</div>
            <h3>Human systems first</h3>
            <p>
              Software is only as good as the human processes around it. Every tool, 
              platform, and AI system operates inside social realities. Plan for human behavior 
              from day one.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="value__card card">
            <div class="value__number">02</div>
            <h3>Governance enables speed</h3>
            <p>
              Good governance is not red tape. It gives teams clear boundaries so they can move 
              quickly without creating chaos. It provides clarity rather than friction.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="value__card card">
            <div class="value__number">03</div>
            <h3>Real participation counts</h3>
            <p>
              Whether running a community or governing an AI deployment, durable solutions require 
              direct user participation. That means listening to feedback, not just running marketing surveys.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="value__card card">
            <div class="value__number">04</div>
            <h3>Practical over impressive</h3>
            <p>
              I share what actually works and what failed in practice. The most valuable operational lessons 
              come from analyzing missteps candidly rather than polishing success stories.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EXPERIENCE TIMELINE -->
    <section class="experience section" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Career background</span></div>
        <h2 id="experience-heading">Where I have worked</h2>

        <div class="timeline">

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">OKX</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">October 2022 to August 2025</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Senior Manager, Global Community Operations</h3>
              <p>Led global community operations and governance across OKX Web3 and CeFi social platforms. Designed content moderation and escalation workflows, managed distributed regional teams across CIS, EU, and SEA, and led an AI-generated community podcast with full governance sign-offs across legal, compliance, and marketing.</p>
              <div class="timeline__tags">
                <span class="badge badge--community">Web3 &amp; CeFi</span>
                <span class="badge badge--ai">Platform Safety</span>
                <span class="badge badge--ai">AI Governance</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">Binance</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">August 2021 to February 2022</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Global Community Program Manager</h3>
              <p>Launched the Binance global Discord community from zero to 40,000+ organic users within six months. Managed high-traffic Telegram ecosystems with millions of global users, implemented retention initiatives, and operationalised the global Binance Angels advocate network.</p>
              <div class="timeline__tags">
                <span class="badge badge--community">Community Architecture</span>
                <span class="badge badge--community">Advocate Programs</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">Google</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">June 2015 to November 2018</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Developer Community Manager, APAC / SEA</h3>
              <p>Led regional developer community programs across APAC/SEA supporting Google Developer Groups (GDG), community leaders, and volunteers across 13 countries. Managed 150+ GDG leaders, oversaw multi-million dollar developer programs, and provided product feedback insights to cross-functional teams.</p>
              <div class="timeline__tags">
                <span class="badge badge--community">Developer Ecosystem</span>
                <span class="badge badge--community">Program Management</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">Wargaming</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">January 2020 to December 2020</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Community Manager, World of Warships (Simplified Chinese)</h3>
              <p>Managed the Simplified Chinese player community for World of Warships on Steam. Conducted sentiment analysis on player trends to guide product updates, resolved bilingual localisation issues across English and Chinese, and managed live community events.</p>
              <div class="timeline__tags">
                <span class="badge badge--community">Gaming</span>
                <span class="badge badge--community">Sentiment Analysis</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">Infocomm Asia Holdings / IAHGames</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">November 2007 to May 2015</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Progressive Operations Leadership (Game Master to Senior Operations Manager)</h3>
              <p>Progressed through seven roles over 8 years. Built and supervised regional cross-country operations teams of 50+ staff across Southeast Asia spanning customer service, product operations, game integrity enforcement, and regional expansion.</p>
              <div class="timeline__tags">
                <span class="badge badge--community">Gaming Operations</span>
                <span class="badge badge--community">Regional Leadership</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline__item">
            <div class="timeline__dot timeline__dot--special"></div>
            <div class="timeline__content">
              <div class="timeline__org-row">
                <span class="timeline__org">Singapore Police Force</span>
                <span class="timeline__period">January 2007 to November 2007</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="timeline__role">Police Officer (Expressway Patrol, Surveillance Camera Unit, Service Quality Branch)</h3>
              <p>Managed incident scenes, investigations, traffic enforcement, and handled public feedback and summon appeals in the Service Quality Branch. Followed by 12.5 years of dedicated National Service.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CREDENTIALS -->
    <section class="credentials section--sm" aria-labelledby="credentials-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label"><span class="label">Qualifications</span></div>
        <h2 id="credentials-heading">Certifications</h2>
        <div class="credentials__grid">
          <div class="credential__card card card--featured">
            <div class="credential__icon">🏛️</div>
            <h3>Certified AI Governance Professional (AIGP)</h3>
            <p>SMU Academy programme, jointly certified with the AI Verify Foundation and endorsed by IMDA. Covers AI risk management frameworks, operational guardrails, and governance alignment with Singapore's MAS AI Risk Management Guidelines and global standards.</p>
            <span class="badge badge--ai" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; display: inline-flex;">AI Governance</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="about-cta section--sm" aria-labelledby="about-cta-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="about-cta__inner card card--featured">
          <h2 id="about-cta-heading">Ready to work together?</h2>
          <p>Whether you need an operational review, AI governance advice, or a speaker for your conference, let's talk.</p>
          <div class="about-cta__buttons">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" id="about-contact-cta">Get in touch →</a>
            <a href="/services" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" id="about-services-cta">View services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.about-page { padding-top: var(--nav-h); }

/* BIO */
.bio__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 380px 1fr; gap: var(--space-16); align-items: start; }
.bio__photo-wrap { border-radius: var(--radius-xl); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border-soft); margin-bottom: var(--space-5); }
.bio__photo-wrap img { width: 100%; height: 520px; object-fit: cover; object-position: center top; }
.bio__social { display: flex; gap: var(--space-3); }
.bio__text-col h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .bio__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .bio__photo-wrap img { height: 380px; }
}

/* VALUES */
.values section { background: var(--bg-surface); }
.values h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); }
.values__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--space-5); }
.value__card { padding: var(--space-8); }
.value__number { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--terracotta); letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.value__card h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.value__card p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .values__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

/* TIMELINE */
.experience h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.timeline { position: relative; padding-left: var(--space-10); }
.timeline::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 7px; top: 8px; bottom: 0;
  width: 1px;
  background: var(--border-soft);
}
.timeline__item { position: relative; margin-bottom: var(--space-10); }
.timeline__item:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.timeline__dot {
  position: absolute;
  left: calc(var(--space-10) * -1 + 1px);
  top: 8px;
  width: 13px; height: 13px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  border: 2px solid var(--border-soft);
  transform: translateX(-50%);
  z-index: 1;
  transition: border-color var(--transition-fast);
}
.timeline__item:hover .timeline__dot { border-color: var(--terracotta); }
.timeline__dot--special { border-color: var(--ochre); background: var(--ochre-glow); }
.timeline__org-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
.timeline__org { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--terracotta); letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.timeline__period { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-faint); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
.timeline__role { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.timeline__content p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.timeline__tags { display: flex; gap: var(--space-2); flex-wrap: wrap; }

/* CREDENTIALS */
.credentials h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
.credentials__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-5); }
.credential__card { padding: var(--space-8); }
.credential__icon { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.credential__card h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
.credential__card p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }

/* CTA */
.about-cta__inner { padding: var(--space-12); text-align: center; }
.about-cta__inner h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
.about-cta__inner p { color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); max-width: 480px; margin-inline: auto; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
.about-cta__buttons { display: flex; gap: var(--space-4); justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
